WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.472
We were headed west, toward the Indian Ocean, and the Nautilus was traveling quickly.

2
00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:23.734
Where would Captain Nemo's whim carry us next? Only time would tell.

3
00:00:23.735 --> 00:00:29.313
Every day we were charmed by some new marvel that we saw through the windows of the submarine.

4
00:00:29.314 --> 00:00:35.893
Ned kept trying to vary our diet by introducing some of the foods we had gathered on our island excursion.

5
00:00:35.894 --> 00:00:41.885
Aside from that, we no longer thought about life on land until something very strange happened.

6
00:00:41.886 --> 00:00:48.052
On January 18, I went up to the platform to greet the day as was my habit.

7
00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:53.964
I waited for the lieutenant to call out his usual phrase, but this time the words were different.

8
00:00:53.965 --> 00:01:01.718
Almost immediately Captain Nemo appeared and scanned the horizon with his telescope. For some minutes he didn't move.

9
00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:08.543
Then he lowered his telescope and exchanged some words with his lieutenant, who appeared agitated.

10
00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:11.456
The captain, however, remained cool.

11
00:01:11.457 --> 00:01:17.440
What had they seen with their telescopes? I looked carefully at the horizon but could see nothing.

12
00:01:17.441 --> 00:01:21.194
The Nautilus was hundreds of miles from the nearest shore.

13
00:01:21.195 --> 00:01:26.178
Pacing the platform, Captain Nemo gave the order for the submarine to speed up.

14
00:01:26.179 --> 00:01:30.195
Just then the lieutenant drew the captain's attention to something.

15
00:01:30.196 --> 00:01:35.257
Captain Nemo stopped pacing and studied the horizon again with his telescope.

16
00:01:35.258 --> 00:01:41.908
I had to find out what they were looking at. I went to the gallery and retrieved a telescope that I often used.

17
00:01:41.909 --> 00:01:48.916
Back on the platform, I raised it to my eye, but as soon as I did that, the telescope was snatched away!

18
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:53.337
I turned around to face Captain Nemo, but I almost didn't recognize him.

19
00:01:53.338 --> 00:01:59.249
His eyes flashed and his teeth were clenched. His whole body betrayed his anger.

20
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.233
He did not move while my telescope rolled at his feet.

21
00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:08.154
Had I unwittingly discovered some secret that provoked this fit of anger?

22
00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:13.488
I quickly realized that I was not the object of his hatred because he wasn't looking at me.

23
00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:17.481
His gaze was fixed on some distant point of the horizon.

24
00:02:17.482 --> 00:02:24.790
"Professor Aronnax," he said in a particularly commanding tone, "I now require you to honor your agreement with me."

25
00:02:24.791 --> 00:02:27.393
"What do you mean?" I asked.

26
00:02:27.394 --> 00:02:32.560
"You and your companions must be confined until I decide to release you."

27
00:02:32.561 --> 00:02:39.290
"You're the captain," I said while looking steadily at him. "But may I ask you one question?"

28
00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.861
"You may not."

29
00:02:40.862 --> 00:02:44.107
It would have been useless to try to resist his order.

30
00:02:44.108 --> 00:02:49.869
I went down to the cabin occupied by Ned and Conseil and told them what the captain had said.

31
00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.448
You can imagine Ned's reaction, but there was no time for argument.

32
00:02:54.449 --> 00:03:00.861
Four of the crew arrived and conducted us to that cell where we had spent our first night onboard the Nautilus.

33
00:03:00.862 --> 00:03:05.099
Ned tried to protest, but the door was shut in his face.

34
00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:09.925
"Master, will you tell us what this all means?" asked Conseil.

35
00:03:09.926 --> 00:03:16.417
I had no idea what was going on and could only think of the strange fear on Captain Nemo's face.

36
00:03:16.418 --> 00:03:20.846
"Hello! What's this?" said Ned, interrupting my thoughts.

37
00:03:20.847 --> 00:03:26.679
"Breakfast! But it's only the regular ship's fare, none of my special treats from the island."

38
00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:32.330
"I suggest we eat it," said Conseil, "because we don't know when we'll see our next meal."

39
00:03:32.331 --> 00:03:39.989
We took our seats at the table and ate in silence. Just then the ceiling light went out, leaving us in total darkness.

40
00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:44.981
"That's all right," said Ned. "I'm feeling sleepy anyway."

41
00:03:44.982 --> 00:03:54.378
To my astonishment both he and Conseil were soon asleep. I was wondering why they were so drowsy when I felt myself becoming very tired.

42
00:03:54.379 --> 00:04:01.799
My eyes closed despite my efforts to keep them open. I began to suspect that our food had been drugged.

43
00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:07.299
Evidently Captain Nemo felt that imprisonment wasn't enough to conceal his actions from us.

44
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:16.799
I heard the hatches shut and thought I felt the Nautilus descending below the surface. I fell into a deep sleep filled with nightmares.

45
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:23.116
The next morning I awoke with a clear head. To my great surprise, I was in my own room.

46
00:04:23.117 --> 00:04:27.118
My companions undoubtedly had been transferred to their cabin.

47
00:04:27.119 --> 00:04:32.118
I tried my door and it opened, so I was once again free to roam the submarine.

48
00:04:32.119 --> 00:04:35.943
I went up on the platform, where I met Ned and Conseil.

49
00:04:35.944 --> 00:04:40.189
Like me, they had been astonished at waking up in their own beds.

50
00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:46.435
The lieutenant came up and pronounced his usual phrase. There was no sign of Captain Nemo.

51
00:04:46.436 --> 00:04:51.348
Later that afternoon I was busy working in the gallery when the captain appeared.

52
00:04:51.349 --> 00:04:59.102
I hoped he might give me some explanation for the previous day's events, but he said nothing. He looked very sad.

53
00:04:59.103 --> 00:05:03.245
After a few minutes he said, "Professor, are you a doctor?"

54
00:05:03.246 --> 00:05:10.483
I was surprised at the question. "Yes, I am. I practiced medicine for several years before I joined the museum."

55
00:05:10.484 --> 00:05:14.737
"Then would you look at one of my men who is ill?"

56
00:05:14.738 --> 00:05:20.991
"Certainly," I said, curious if this man's illness had anything to do with yesterday's mysterious happenings.

57
00:05:20.992 --> 00:05:24.483
Captain Nemo led me to a cabin near the crew's quarters.

58
00:05:24.484 --> 00:05:30.515
On the bed lay a man who was not only seriously ill but also gravely wounded.

59
00:05:30.516 --> 00:05:36.578
His head was covered with a bandage, and when I unwrapped it, I found a devastating injury.

60
00:05:36.579 --> 00:05:40.388
"What caused this wound?" I asked.

61
00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:43.650
"Does it really matter? How is he doing?"

62
00:05:43.651 --> 00:05:50.047
I hesitated to give my opinion, but Nemo reassured me that the man couldn't understand me if I spoke French.

63
00:05:50.048 --> 00:05:54.896
"He'll be dead in two hours," I said. "Nothing can be done to save him."

64
00:05:54.897 --> 00:06:01.801
I was surprised to see tears glistening in Captain Nemo's eyes. He said, "You may go now, Professor."

65
00:06:01.802 --> 00:06:10.626
For the rest of the day I felt upset. I slept badly that night and thought I heard distant music that sounded like a funeral hymn.

66
00:06:10.627 --> 00:06:16.531
The next morning Captain Nemo asked if my companions and I could go for another underwater walk.

67
00:06:16.532 --> 00:06:21.936
This time Ned decided to go with us because he regretted having missed our underwater hunt.

68
00:06:21.937 --> 00:06:26.952
Accompanied by Captain Nemo and about a dozen crew members, we left the Nautilus.

69
00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:31.936
I recognized at once that we were in the middle of a kingdom made of coral.

70
00:06:31.937 --> 00:06:35.611
Four of the men were carrying an oblong-shaped object.

71
00:06:35.612 --> 00:06:43.920
After walking for about two hours, we came to an area where there was a coral cross surrounded by small mounds of coral.

72
00:06:43.921 --> 00:06:47.182
Obviously the cross and mounds were man-made.

73
00:06:47.183 --> 00:06:50.920
And then it occurred to me that we were in the middle of a cemetery.

74
00:06:50.921 --> 00:06:55.658
The oblong object was the body of the man who had died the previous night.

75
00:06:55.659 --> 00:07:04.245
A grave was dug and the man was buried with great care and ceremony. Back onboard the Nautilus, I talked to Captain Nemo.

76
00:07:04.246 --> 00:07:07.237
"That was the man who died last night," I said.

77
00:07:07.238 --> 00:07:16.729
"Yes, now the coral will do its work and cover him for eternity." Nemo buried his face in his hands and tried to suppress a sob.

78
00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:20.721
"Your dead sleep out of the reach of sharks," I said quietly.

79
00:07:20.722 --> 00:07:26.921
"Yes, sir, of sharks and men," gravely replied the captain.
